Subject: [PATCH] liblinphone/wrappers/python: honor LINPHONESDK_VERSION env

Base: upstream linphone-sdk commit 7d5fe98a18ff7be2381656b600f880e3c49f5089
      (master, 2025-12-23), vendored under third_party/linphone-sdk/.

This patch is applied automatically by poc-linphone/scripts/build_linphone_sdk.sh
before configuring the SDK build, and reverted after the build completes. The
linphone-sdk source tree is otherwise untouched.

Why this patch exists
=====================

liblinphone/wrappers/python/genwrapper.py shells out to `git describe`
to read the version string that gets baked into the generated Python
wrapper. When the SDK is vendored as a subtree under
poc-linphone/third_party/linphone-sdk/, that directory has no .git of
its own, so the subprocess call exits with `fatal: not a git
repository` and brings the whole build down.

This patch makes genwrapper.py honour LINPHONESDK_VERSION from the
environment before falling back to `git describe`. The build script
exports it to match -DLINPHONESDK_VERSION on the cmake command line.

---
 liblinphone/wrappers/python/genwrapper.py | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/liblinphone/wrappers/python/genwrapper.py b/liblinphone/wrappers/python/genwrapper.py
--- a/liblinphone/wrappers/python/genwrapper.py
+++ b/liblinphone/wrappers/python/genwrapper.py
@@ -628,7 +628,11 @@ def renderClassFile(path, item, renderer):

 if __name__ == '__main__':
     import subprocess
+    # PoC patch: honor caller-provided version; skip the git describe
+    # probe that fails when this tree is embedded in another repo
+    # (e.g. as a vendored subtree under third_party/).
+    git_version = os.environ.get("LINPHONESDK_VERSION", "").strip().encode() or \
+                  subprocess.check_output(["git", "describe"]).strip()
-    git_version = subprocess.check_output(["git", "describe"]).strip()

     argparser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description='Generate source files for the Python wrapper')
     argparser.add_argument('xmldir', type=str, help='Directory where the XML documentation of the Linphone\'s API generated by Doxygen is placed')
